# Save actions

## Inline / card editors (expansion panels, StandardCard `#actions`)

- Primary label is always **`Save`** — never “Save tour”, “Save screen”, or other compound labels.
- **`Save` is disabled until the form is dirty** (local draft differs from the last loaded/saved baseline).
- Do **not** add a Cancel next to Save. Discard by collapsing the panel (reset draft) or leaving without saving.

```vue
<v-btn
  color="primary"
  variant="elevated"
  :loading="saving"
  :disabled="!dirty"
  @click="save"
>
  Save
</v-btn>
```

## Dialogs

Cancel + primary remain correct — Cancel dismisses the modal without committing.

```vue
<template #actions>
  <v-spacer />
  <v-btn variant="text" class="mr-2" @click="close">Cancel</v-btn>
  <v-btn color="primary" variant="elevated" @click="save">Save</v-btn>
</template>
```
